  "live_records": {
    "q-111525": {
      "dom_id": "step-q111525",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.4$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ |\n\nLet $Y=X-4.$ The distribution of $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $y$ | $-4$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $c$ | $d$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $a$ | $b$ | $0.3$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ |\n\nWhat is the value of $a+c+d?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's add a $Y=X-4$ row to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-4$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.4$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, ${f}_{X}(x)={f}_{Y}(y)$ for corresponding values of $X$ and $Y.$ Therefore, the distribution of $Y$ is as follows:\n\n| $y$ | $-4$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.4$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ |\n\nSo, we have $a=0.4,c=-1,d=0,$ and therefore $a+c+d=-0.6.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
