    "q-111521": {
      "dom_id": "step-q111521",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $0.5$ | $1$ | $1.5$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.3$ |\n\nLet $Y=4X-3.$ The distribution of $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $y$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $a$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.15$ | $b$ | $c$ | $0.25$ | $d$ |\n\nWhat is the value of $a+b+d?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's add a $Y=4X-3$ row to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $0.5$ | $1$ | $1.5$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.3$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, ${f}_{X}(x)={f}_{Y}(y)$ for corresponding values of $X$ and $Y.$ Therefore, the distribution of $Y$ is as follows:\n\n| $y$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.3$ |\n\nSo, we have $a=3,b=0.2,d=0.3,$ and therefore $a+b+d=3.5.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
