    "q-149769": {
      "dom_id": "step-q149769",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{2}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ |\n\nLet $Y=\\frac{X}{2}-4.$ Calculate $P(Y=-2).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's add a $Y=\\frac{X}{2}-4$ row to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-4$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{2}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ |\n\nNow, ${f}_{X}(x)={f}_{Y}(y)$ for corresponding values of $X$ and $Y.$ Therefore, the distribution of $Y$ is as follows:\n\n| $y$ | $-4$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{2}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $P(Y=-2)=\\frac{2}{5}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
